light:

  rect 2 4 5 5 5        ; start chamber -- lit, safe, nothing can reach you
  rect 7 6 5 1 1        ; ...into the dark. the rhythm starts here
  rect 8 5 1 1 3
  rect 10 7 1 1 3
  rect 12 3 14 11 5     ; HALL A opens up and brightens
  rect 17 1 3 2 7       ; the glow alcove: brightest thing on the level
  cell 18 1 7
  cell 24 14 3
  rect 23 15 2 4 1      ; dark again
  rect 14 19 13 6 6     ; EXIT HALL -- brightest room
  rect 19 24 3 1 7
  rect 23 26 5 3 4      ; secret vault
end

notes:

THE VESTIBULE -- teach the verbs, then let the player use them.

  1 SPAWN (4,6) facing east in a small lit chamber with one column in it, so
    the very first frame already shows a near face, a far face and a floor.
    The only opening is a bright slot in the east wall. Teaches: forward.
  2 THE CORRIDOR (x7-11 y6, light 1). One cell wide and dark, with two 1-deep
    alcoves at (8,5) and (10,7) that break the wall silhouette as you pass --
    the cheapest possible way to make walking read as motion.
  3 HALL A (x12-25 y3-13, light 5). The corridor dumps you out at (12,6),
    which is deliberately BETWEEN the column rows at y5 and y8 rather than
    on a clear axis: the first frame in the hall is two rows of columns
    opening diagonally away from you, which is the most three-dimensional
    image this engine can draw. Twelve columns on a 3-cell pitch turn a
    14x11 room into something with depth from every standing position.
  4 THE GLOW ALCOVE (x17-19 y2) holds the SHOTGUN, lit at 7 against a level
    that averages 2. It is the brightest thing you have seen and it is off
    the main aisle: reward visible from the entrance, one detour to take it.
    Landmark #1.
  5 FIRST HUSK at (23,10), the far corner, ~11 cells away and behind columns.
    It has to walk an aisle to reach you, so you see it coming and the whole
    hall plus the corridor is behind you to back into. Safe-ish first kill.
  6 The columns are the teaching tool: with no strafe, a 1x1 pillar is the
    only cover the game has, and the 2-cell aisles make circling one work.
  7 DOOR (24,14), south-east, reached down the x24 aisle -- the aisle points
    at it, so the route is signposted by the architecture, not a map.
  8 DESCENT (x24 y15-18, light 1) with a medkit in a recess at (23,17).
    Tight and dark after the open hall: the rhythm again.
  9 EXIT HALL (x14-26 y19-24, light 6) -- brightest room on the level, eight
    columns, two husks. You enter at (24,19) beside a column, so the reveal
    is a diagonal through the colonnade rather than a flat wall. The exit
    switch (glow, x19-21 y25) is visible from the doorway.
 10 SECRET: the wall at (25,25) is a fake. Armour and a shell box behind it.
end
